id: pm-csv-bounded-admission
title: Admit large CSV imports within declared memory and mutation budgets
description: "Stream initial or full validation before import commitment. Acceptance: a million-row fixture stays under a declared heap cap independent of file size; invalid final rows prevent atomic application; exact counts are distinguished from upper bounds. Reuse CSV mapping and SDK schema/status/transaction capabilities rather than introducing a dialect or journal."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T03:16:17.816Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T06:28:22.781Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Bounded million-row validation; late invalid rows cause zero atomic writes; exact and bounded estimates; typed SDK and compact CLI; no-git real-data validation; seeded state tests and npm/Bun release gates
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T03:17:36.890Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core public SDK exposes schema/status registries, complete reads and mutation/transaction primitives but no streaming CSV resource admission contract. pm-csv already owns parsing, mapping, schema negotiation and atomic import; pm-beads owns JSONL reconciliation and pm-todos owns todo files. This change adds bounded initial/full resource receipts and an opt-in atomic admission guard, reusing shared row validation. No dialect or journal is introduced. Workspace transactions do not isolate ordinary writers; existing per-write SDK rereads remain required and the final read/write window remains documented."
  "2026-10-29T03:29:52.640Z",codex-agent,"Implemented read-only csv admit and typed admitCSV with exact full counts, conservative initial lower bounds, mutation upper bounds, fixed field/record/column allocations, SHA-256 source binding and settings drift refusal. Atomic import can opt into the same full pass with --admission; only bounded bytes are materialized and source drift refuses before parsing. Targeted regressions cover late invalid rows, custom status normalization, finite limit fuzzing, all parser split points and every source/settings admission boundary. Million-row fixture is 163000015 bytes; final heap-cap rerun is pending."
  "2026-10-29T03:50:32.261Z",codex-agent,"Measured public origin/main tracker in a scratch non-git directory: 133 items, 133 exported/admitted rows, 46572 CSV bytes, zero invalid rows, maximum field width 2946 code units; full scan 47 ms and 57801136 bytes observed heap. Warmed only SDK-derived caches before making the copy read-only; all tracked bytes and all copied file hashes remained unchanged during measurement. Million-row fixture: 163000015 source bytes under --max-old-space-size=96 --max-semi-space-size=4, V8 heap limit 113246208 bytes (below declared 128 MiB), observed heap about 31.5 MB. Added revision-bound admitted steps, current SDK history checks including ABA, certified SDK list reads and source/settings interleaving tests; ordinary-writer final read/write window remains explicit."
  "2026-10-29T05:11:32.568Z",codex-agent,"Completed native admitted-write hardening: explicit SDK identities and revision-bound steps, deterministic peer identity adoption, per-invocation write counts, SDK semantic preview before any target application, source-based scope selection shared with legacy import, and configured-status filter normalization. Tests cover ordinary writers at inspection/capture/apply boundaries, keyed-creation races, peer edits during compensation, ABA replays, deleted targets, malformed retained bindings, all status roles and an empty executable PATH. Initial observation counts blank records toward its budget and remains non-authorizing at EOF. Public minimum SDK artifact 2026.8.20 has complete reads and status roles but lacks semantic preview and transaction-key derivation; read-only admission remains supported, while admitted application returns a typed upgrade remedy on such hosts. No dependency pin was changed."
  "2026-10-29T06:11:17.637Z",codex-agent,"Verification: the linked pm test command was run through pm test --run --progress --timeout 900 --shared-host-safe --fail-on-skipped --fail-on-empty-test-run: 25 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled, including 500 seeded sequences and 2000 operations. Automatic test evidence recording is disabled by the existing project policy, so the result is recorded here without changing settings. A subsequent focused admission/parser/atomic/command regression run passed 165 tests with zero skips; admission.ts measured 100% lines, branches and functions. Lint, typecheck, test compilation, docstrings and duplication checks passed. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates will run in CI."
  "2026-10-29T06:11:55.600Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof used a disposable non-git copy, never the reviewed checkout. The fixed baseline passed both selected regressions; removing only StreamingCSVParser.appendField allocation guards made the field/record resource test fail, and disabling only importCSV admission dispatch made the late-invalid-row zero-write test fail. Restoring each implementation made its selected regression pass again. The reviewed source hashes stayed unchanged. Refreshed overlap against the public 2026.10.28 SDK found only in-memory mutation parsing/document resolution, no streaming admission surface; sibling package and upstream issue searches found no duplicate contract. Final read-only public tracker measurement: 133 items and exact rows, 46572 CSV bytes, zero invalid rows, maximum field width 2946 code units, mutation upper bound 133, 52 ms, 44049096 bytes observed heap; all copied file hashes unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T06:22:11.117Z",codex-agent,"Expanded state evidence passed: 500 seeded operation sequences, 2000 operations, 386 exports and 48 complete export/import/replay round trips. Every comparison reads actual native SDK state against independent SDK reference transitions; peer edits after replay refuse older inputs and retain relationships/scope. Packed validation exposed a known older-host preview limitation: SDK 2026.10.25 treats installed dependency links as tracker storage, while a fresh packed CLI install and guarded application succeed on the current 2026.10.28 host. The public preview signature accepts only pmRoot/transactionId/author/mutations and no storage-exclusion override; no custom snapshot or validation bypass is added. Added an actionable typed host/storage remedy, retained the dependency pin, and expanded packed acceptance to npm/Bun current project-local, global and npx/bunx contexts. Strict health passes with an isolated global package registry; the ambient registry reports an unrelated pm-github host-version skew."
  "2026-10-29T06:28:16.477Z",codex-agent,"Final local acceptance: npm run accept:packed passed all nine scenarios. Six current 2026.10.28 contexts (npm/Bun project-local, npm/Bun global, npx and bunx) completed guarded native application and importer replay with zero new replay writes. The three legacy/minimum-host contexts passed their existing package acceptance and read-only admission; guarded application returned the typed upgrade remedy with no target created. The final native-validation/remedy regression passed 1/1. Dependency and 100% coverage thresholds are unchanged. Implementation, docs, public-copy metrics, state property evidence and behavioral revert proof are ready for review; full npm and Bun release gates remain delegated to the exact-head CI run."
